      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Group 1 (alkali metals) and Group 2 (alkaline earth metals) are both reactive metals, but they differ because of their ionization energies. A Group 1 metal has only one electron to lose and readily forms a +1 ion; a Group 2 metal must lose two electrons, which needs more energy, so it is reactive but generally less so than the Group 1 metal of the same period. In both groups reactivity increases down the group as atoms grow and ionization energy falls."
          },
          {
